(collectively, the "Work") are made available to a closed, named set of
individuals and organisations (the "Authorised Recipients") solely for the
purposes set out in Section 2 below. Any other use — including but not limited
to copying, forking, publishing, sublicensing, selling, training other models
on the Work, or making the Work available to anyone who is not an Authorised
Recipient — requires prior written permission from all Copyright Holders named
above. See Section 6 for the contact address.


================================================================================
1.  DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1 "Work" means the entirety of the contents of this repository at any given
    commit, including without limitation:

      a. all source code, configuration, scripts, schemas, migrations and
         fixtures;
      b. all documentation under `docs/`, `openspec/`, `README.md`, and any
         other prose or diagrams;
      c. all data files, built catalogues, snapshots, transcriptions, audio
         samples, benchmark corpora and any derivatives of the source
         datasets (`docs/sources/bodegas-y-stock.xlsx`,
         `docs/sources/discovery-consolidado.xlsx`, etc.);
      d. all prompts, model configurations, fine-tuning artefacts, evaluation
         harnesses and the contents of `benchmarks/`, `spikes/` and the
         `services/` workspaces;
      e. all design decisions, requirement IDs, scenarios and rationale
         captured in the OpenSpec deliverables and in any
         `openspec/changes/*` directory.

1.2 "Authorised Recipients" means, **and only** means, the following natural
    persons and legal entities, taken collectively:

      a. Braejan David Arias Heregua
      b. Daniel Rosas
      c. Adriana Durand (Invitado) — <adriana.durandc@gmail.com>
      d. Edith Lavado             — <edith.lavado04@gmail.com>
      e. Daniel Rosas             — <danielrosas.business@gmail.com>
      f. 30X
      g. Colsubsidio

    The email addresses above are associated with the named individuals for
    identification only; this Licence does not grant any rights to any other
    person who happens to share such an email address, and the absence of an
    email address for a natural person does not exclude that person from the
    list.

1.3 "Authorised Purpose" means the development, demonstration, evaluation and
    judging of the Voice Inventory Counter MVP for the Hospitality Challenge
    of the Colsubsidio x 30X hackathon in July 2026, and any continuation,
    integration or hand-off of that work that occurs **between** the
    Authorised Recipients named above.

1.4 "Personal Data" has the meaning given to it by Ley 1581 of 2012
    (Colombia) and any successor regulation, and includes the dictated audio,
    transcripts, product names, and any data that can be linked to an
    identifiable operator or auditor.


