================================================================================
4.  PERSONAL DATA, AUDIO AND PROVENANCE
================================================================================

4.1 The Work contains, or is designed to process, Personal Data that belongs
    to Colsubsidio's operators and auditors. An Authorised Recipient who
    handles such data MUST comply with the Privacy and security notes in
    `README.md` and with the requirements RF-04, RF-12, RF-13, RNF-04,
    RNF-05, RNF-13 and RNF-14 of the PRD.

4.2 Voice is not stored by design. If, during the Authorised Purpose, an
    Authorised Recipient needs to record, transcribe or replay voice audio
    (for example, to evaluate a transcript), that Authorised Recipient MUST
    obtain the speaker's informed consent, anonymise the recording where
    possible, and delete the recording as soon as the evaluation is complete.

4.3 The source datasets under `docs/sources/` are vendored from the
    Colsubsidio x 30X discovery process. They are NOT covered by the grant
    in Section 2 to the extent they contain Personal Data; an Authorised
    Recipient MUST handle them under the same rule as 4.2.


